{"event_type":"review","id":"faa13bbeed44c5dd413dadceb710fcec5329255e22fc0c79d560dd2331e9d871","occurred_at":"2026-11-07T22:04:33Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/058012be964b36709d356ab65256cd5abc66eb15033561d078a793947be081d6","sha256":"058012be964b36709d356ab65256cd5abc66eb15033561d078a793947be081d6"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/a96ec8941429ca81ddc3e6182a4b52fa5f48484fee9420311f479c05d95d1e6b","sha256":"a96ec8941429ca81ddc3e6182a4b52fa5f48484fee9420311f479c05d95d1e6b"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/8bcabce5b4ba23ecd4b42fdc7bf608245938d836cedbddd8ec06f9846d2c90b0","sha256":"8bcabce5b4ba23ecd4b42fdc7bf608245938d836cedbddd8ec06f9846d2c90b0"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/0a24f612f48d952707ec9962e8487ac0b40ab37e70f504a083ebc1bdc968d84b","sha256":"0a24f612f48d952707ec9962e8487ac0b40ab37e70f504a083ebc1bdc968d84b"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/4db14f1be7ef834a4127d087ba889c6901f6e2710c4b0a5d19a4da6228a2ffac","sha256":"4db14f1be7ef834a4127d087ba889c6901f6e2710c4b0a5d19a4da6228a2ffac"}],"attempt_id":"8bb49917ff7ededecd586d2eebb35c9f91327c97a2fb6c1aca7763eb1483611f:0:1","base":"4b51c51314bd37c858eea3ce5b00d6e2468bce92","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"55c91b75d3c06caa0d5d81655172f39ff79a8d6f","body":"**Root path derivation breaks on Windows and in paths with special characters.**\n\n`new URL('..', import.meta.url).pathname` yields a URL-encoded path. On Windows it yields `/C:/...`. On a checkout path with spaces, it yields `%20`. In both cases `needsDist` fails: `readFileSync` cannot open the file, and the test throws. The CLI-filter test at Line 93 already normalizes Windows separators, so cross-platform use appears intended. Use `fileURLToPath` instead.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-import { join } from 'node:path';\n+import { join } from 'node:path';\n+import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\n...\n-  const root = new URL('..', import.meta.url).pathname;\n+  const root = fileURLToPath(new URL('..', import.meta.url));\n```\n</details>","id":"0024e547cae5edf916632a45303e1dfa0e019fd15f85f591c04b449c10fe3227","intervals":[],"path":"test/global-setup.test.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Root path derivation breaks on Windows and in paths with special characters."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"8f3754f703356d4ab3f1cb03f15c5ee195e53ebe","body":"**Reject empty evidence and line numbers below 1 in `evidenceFailure`.**\n\nThe comment at Lines 1701-1706 says an unchanged answer is posted only when every cited location exists. Two inputs currently pass this check without proving anything:\n- `evidence: []` skips the loop and returns `null`. The reply is posted with an empty `Evidence:` line, and the next run treats the thread as settled.\n- A `line` of 0, a negative number, or a non-integer passes `line > lines.length`, even on an empty blob.\n\n`FixReviewItemResult.evidence` says \"at least one entry for `unchanged_with_reason`\" (src/ops/review/fixReviewItem.ts:204-234). The parser may already enforce this. Even so, this gate is the last check before a settling reply is posted, so it should enforce the rule itself.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n   if (!COMMIT_SHA_RE.test(tip)) {\n     return 'the worktree tip is unreadable';\n   }\n+  if (evidence.length === 0) {\n+    return 'no evidence cited';\n+  }\n   for (const { path, line } of evidence) {\n+    if (!Number.isSafeInteger(line) || line < 1) {\n+      return `${path}:${String(line)} is not a valid line`;\n+    }\n     // A FILE, not a tree: `git show <tip>:<dir>` succeeds on a directory too.\n```\n</details>","id":"652cb918602a5bbaf1eecaf906aeff0f68d071b2b679ba5ec2985632399b58b8","intervals":[],"path":"src/plans/review-loop.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Reject empty evidence and line numbers below 1 in `evidenceFailure`."}],"head":"615aeca42fa2728f3c0d78cc7098c73fff748b79","head_tree":"067d49da10942551a3c39da201ad1d79467f9afa","input_scope":[{"blob":"8f3754f703356d4ab3f1cb03f15c5ee195e53ebe","intervals":[[9,9],[12,15],[76,82],[100,102],[108,109],[112,113],[115,116],[118,120],[156,311],[371,372],[381,383],[411,416],[472,492],[495,497],[502,517],[522,523],[545,547],[550,558],[585,594],[702,705],[799,848],[941,947],[951,971],[980,1028],[1071,1147],[1168,1173],[1177,1179],[1195,1197],[1199,1293],[1295,1295],[1326,1326],[1336,1336],[1343,1358],[1531,1541],[1544,1551],[1554,1556],[1558,1562],[1570,1574],[1578,1587],[1597,1597],[1600,1600],[1602,1618],[1670,1676],[1678,1722],[1724,1724],[1783,1784],[1790,1793],[1801,1801],[1813,1813],[1833,1834],[1845,1845]],"path":"src/plans/review-loop.ts"},{"blob":"b676bb94615936572dde70163a0e023acfadaad2","intervals":[[17,18],[22,43],[71,85],[88,93],[96,104],[204,209],[255,258],[260,275],[314,315],[318,393],[435,438],[522,530],[533,544],[558,565],[583,583],[642,642],[652,652],[659,660],[677,677],[679,679],[696,697],[699,706],[715,716],[718,721],[725,727],[735,866],[871,884],[886,903],[905,958],[960,960],[963,963],[968,1042]],"path":"src/selfhost/self-review-loop.ts"},{"blob":"55c91b75d3c06caa0d5d81655172f39ff79a8d6f","intervals":[[2,5],[7,7],[22,37],[49,99]],"path":"test/global-setup.test.ts"}],"job_id":"8bb49917ff7ededecd586d2eebb35c9f91327c97a2fb6c1aca7763eb1483611f:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"entry":{"blob":"b654976307e26f6499edd58293d4cc991e81b9fc","kind":"blob","mode":"100644","path":"src/selfhost/self-review-loop.ts"},"merge":"d8da1e2f8a592f1858a1bf97cb04a729ce9f6d3b","method":"pre-merge","pre":"34401d741bd653d722472f4e99a1dca6040433ce","source_path":"src/selfhost/self-review-loop.ts"},"blob":"b676